{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I will come down.</b> This is one of ten descents written in the Torah (there)." "<b>And I will speak with you.</b> And not with them (there)." "<b>And I will take.</b> As its Targum: 'וַאֲרַבֵּי' — as in ״וְאֶל אֲצִילֵי בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ (Exodus 24)." "<b>And I will set upon them.</b> To what is Moses compared at that moment? To a lamp set upon a menorah, from which all kindle and its light lacks nothing (Sifrei)." "<b>And they shall bear with you.</b> Stipulate with them on condition that they accept upon themselves the burden of My children — for they are burdensome and obstinate (there)." "<b>And you shall not bear it alone.</b> This is an answer to what you said: ״I cannot, I alone״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:27.461576814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}